  "final_message": "Refunding a paid invoice now finds the customer's successful payments. The 24 tests pass. I didn't add a test for this case.\n\n**Root cause:** `refund_invoice` in `billing/refunds.py` called `successful_payments(ctx, invoice[\"customer_id\"])`. That function looks payments up by invoice id (`payments_for_invoice`), so passing a customer id matched nothing. The refund loop never ran. With no account credit applied, `refunded_total` stayed 0 and it raised \"invoice has no successful payment to refund\".\n\n**Fix:** it now passes `invoice_id`.\n\nI wrote `answer.json` in the repo root:\n```json\n{\"file\": \"refunds.py\", \"function\": \"refund_invoice\"}\n```",
